**Convention 1.2 (reused results and the additional instance).** SSA
Theorem 12.1 supplies the sufficient structural reference: byte switches,
tape spines, maintained head links, finite guarded atomic patches and four
individual kernels on its original actual image. RCA Theorems 15.2–15.3
supply the actual installed, acquired and callable historical service,
conditional on its permissions, canonical code supply and finite completion.
Neither theorem is asserted anew as a general replay or acquisition result.

The additional instance constructed here consists of three compatible
interfaces: storage and construction of RCA's actual finite control
versions; extraction of the activation choice and all variable input during
every installation and service phase; and a reversible structural
interpretation of the actual HistoricalImage wire output. Sections 3–7
discharge those interfaces rather than assuming that the two supplier
domains coincide. NCR's restricted fixed-controller, atomic-source result
retains its original hypotheses and is not enlarged by a source-only inverse.

